}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Literature", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9656476497407303`*^9, 3.965647662007294*^9}, {
  3.966064507573797*^9, 
  3.966064512039612*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a04bec9-2e88-4971-8bea-\
b7d27075706c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["LeanDojo", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965020687491251*^9, 
  3.965020692485338*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6fcde837-68b8-40bb-a065-\
6652412b03b4"],

Cell["\<\
It is not necessary that the tool would be a Lean plugin that suggests \
tactics. Maybe natural language is a better encoding? However, we can \
rephrase lean proofs as natural language and then input that into Chat GPT \
(so there\[CloseCurlyQuote]s an injection in natural language). This already \
has been done in Lean Dojo. So we can look at that.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965021946098837*^9, 3.965021992009715*^9}, {
   3.965022094068252*^9, 3.965022156836722*^9}, 3.9650229969471703`*^9, {
   3.96504854162807*^9, 
   3.9650485719169817`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9d2f26a5-0ea3-4985-a7f7-\
20c9c5c40efd"],

Cell["\<\
For instance, Zorn\[CloseCurlyQuote]s lemma is used a lot in these proofs. \
Also, the first isomorphism theorem. So are these proofs analagous to \
sentences in the English language which are commonly used? But here we are \
trying to do something indeed. So let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s see. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965023170645208*^9, 3.965023204992515*^9}, {
  3.9650235193797407`*^9, 3.965023569203293*^9}, {3.967101739441608*^9, 
  3.967101739534322*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"18491591-1e9b-41c8-a814-\
b566a2355cdb"],

Cell["https://arxiv.org/pdf/2306.15626", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.966064500618661*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a51ef36d-1ed4-4906-9467-\
f2b54304e38c"],

Cell["All we need is attention basically.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969686067264189*^9, 
  3.9696860708871326`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b391a998-1c2e-4255-a283-\
ed9857dbd098"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["HTPS", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965020776440086*^9, 
  3.965020777047694*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"517581d8-ba0f-4bbf-adac-\
80f4a72c4412"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Alpha Proof: When RL meets formal mathematics", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9650225347654753`*^9, 
  3.965022544993974*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"69cebde2-5f2b-472f-8ae6-\
99657d83138a"],

Cell["\<\
