 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965048870583441*^9, 3.965048871840776*^9}, {
  3.965048902369976*^9, 
  3.965048904067645*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c457c9a8-b697-4900-9288-\
e417bcfed078"],

Cell["https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphageometry", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965624950798189*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a269fc00-b2fd-47d1-976f-\
58489a475fa6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The zero philosophy", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965049061199779*^9, 
  3.965049064265369*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6a54cb61-d398-4f99-acd1-\
4e4ac7948220"],

Cell["\<\
If an agent can learn to master an environment tabula rasa, then you \
demonstrably have a system that is discovering and learning new knowledge by \
itself.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9650490704380503`*^9, 
  3.965049073925378*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef3b69f6-f80c-4773-a955-\
5c015b778141"],

Cell["\<\
AlphaGoZero and AlphaZero learned simply by playing games against itself, \
starting from completely random play. Rediscovered human patterns, \
accumulating thousands of years of human knowledge in a matter of days. \
Ultimately discarded some in preference of new discoveries that humans don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t even know about.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96504909776858*^9, 
  3.9650491523408747`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9294b265-4368-4c33-81bc-\
ffc4f452c1f0"],

Cell["\<\
I mean I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t how these reinforcement learning algorithms \
worked? It might be cool to see how that worked for the case of games etc.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9653047511826477`*^9, 
  3.965304772633522*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c2ff6088-b54a-4666-a5dc-\
526f948ea43e"],

Cell["\<\
So why did these games and everything were so successful? Well, there was \
scaled up trial and error, grounded feedback signal, and search. This means \
the systems could play games against themselves and can try/lose many things. \
There is a grounded feedback signal, which is basically losing/winning the \
game. So here in the case of proving things, lean is perfect because it can \
easily just verify the proof. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965304682280054*^9, 3.965304774529871*^9}, {
  3.9653048171262197`*^9, 
  3.965304851661786*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cce5bdfe-aa27-4c5a-8b84-\
fd5ee19ba184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lean gives us a way to ",
 StyleBox["scale up trial and error ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "with\na. An ",
 StyleBox["environment ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "to explore mathematics completely in silico\nb. A ",
 StyleBox["perfect feedback ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "signal for proving"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9653048871391077`*^9, 
  3.965304919924893*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"33b6d172-d7a0-409a-9b89-\
6353590e7034"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can therefore ",
 StyleBox["reach superhuman intelligence and discover new truths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", just like there, provided:\n1. We can generate high enough quality + \
quantity problems\n2. RL works."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96530492129492*^9, 
  3.96530495204331*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"53ce9052-26c0-48d9-ba32-\
e8cdf043845b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Okay. Seems to me that this reinforcement learning paradigm works but it\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s focused on IMO problems etc. and isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
focusing on the ",
 StyleBox["language ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "part. In my opinion, just how LLMs were made, we can focus on how this \
algebra thing works."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965305404819845*^9, 3.965305456994635*^9}, 
   3.965608457254085*^9},ExpressionUUID->"611c5ef9-ab97-4ee0-b733-\
55f9475ba356"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Formalizer model", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965647191737089*^9, 3.965647194658446*^9}, 
   3.970896965335187*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4fe402d2-20a7-4d02-9cf6-\
a32ccd85503b"],

Cell["\<\
Input is a problem described in natural language. And then the output is a \
lean formalization of the problem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965647196602191*^9, 
  3.965647221919325*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ef39965-50e1-4921-925d-\
f9b639fb715c"],

Cell["So here we are doing actions i.e. over lean tactics.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965647254582191*^9, 
  3.965647263438271*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fff185ad-1c66-4d74-9a82-\
f8c2a3d31b33"],

Cell["\<\
Challenges for alpha proof: inherited challenges from formal mathematics. \
Most of the human data is in natural langauge. Cannot easily learn and work \
on areas not supported by Mathlib.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965647524444467*^9, 3.965647546592493*^9}, {
  3.965647595316284*^9, 
  3.965647615912303*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e93c753-4e97-4b29-940e-\
1dd222bb96f5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Functional programming in Lean", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965221624837191*^9, 
  3.9652216297065163`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4274df7a-8571-4f2e-96a4-\
fc64a55ab31a"],

Cell["\<\
There is stuff like BHK interpretation etc. which may be important for a \
theoretical understanding here.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965624521273641*^9, 
  3.965624542192079*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"85471e48-2f87-49e6-ae06-\
4a38b01f4830"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So here an expression ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "98eaf394-f1bf-4c58-a34e-871028149652"],
 " is a correct proof of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "492157ba-9eb2-425b-b59b-0ce9343c6c8e"],
 " means that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2010612e-0821-48bb-bbc3-886eb47d9cac"],
 " has type ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Proof", " ", "p"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0214190-2f48-4d69-9c8a-dde632fe8e1d"],
 ". So here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e69742f-bfa0-43dd-8b5e-08d94afcd7a3"],
 " is a proposition and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Proof", " ", "p"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3243a908-cf04-413e-b798-6b7fac71c287"],
 " is a new type, the type of proof of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "84bade4e-c3d6-4dc3-9890-5fa4abfbdd09"],
 ". So this is a type constructor. However, we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t need \
this. We can say that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "97065ae1-58b4-42a5-b384-acc45390b5b7"],
 " is a proposition and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdef054d-8f24-4d57-a9ae-f8d948a2e9c5"],
 " is of type ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "65aa6576-f40f-4e75-a6e0-12fa87e0b8bc"],
 " iff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdac5848-989f-43ae-9f2b-811cb7c8eac7"],
 " is a proof of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d2380a8-8615-4e6b-aa28-c0df1769f3e9"],
 ". Also ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"->", " "}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "de02eb45-bfdc-439d-937e-e1fd6a36c153"],
 " is a type constructor where if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fa643696-9a6c-4b12-810b-74e3c4006185"],
 " is prop, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["q", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f2faa6ca-b996-4380-9cc2-fa56bd537a36"],
 " is prop, then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", " ", "->", " ", "q"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e5d66d1-584d-4489-a4bd-426fc353471c"],
 " is also a  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["Prop", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a057c0a2-e07f-4910-bc5f-cf047836584c"],
 " i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"q", " ", ":", " ", "Prop"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "22e947a0-9dae-40a4-b020-0bb7612002c6"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9656086398785458`*^9, 3.965608641972459*^9}, {
  3.9656087958241053`*^9, 3.965608874915057*^9}, {3.965608907860614*^9, 
  3.9656089614724197`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"543be67a-47a3-4804-b77d-\
f9399f90291f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lean is a strict pure functional language with dependent types ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "aaf5b980-42e3-44a4-a7c1-f334ebfcb516"],
 " just like Agda which uses Haskell."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965221729560978*^9, 
  3.965221788303987*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"243a9616-ee7d-4ea9-a7ea-\
e302dff4af38"],

Cell["\<\
elan manages the Lean compiler toolchains, similarly to rustup or ghcup.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965221990754304*^9},ExpressionUUID->"13e1ae0a-2c9c-4367-93e7-\
f525d5df5451"],

Cell["\<\
lake builds Lean packages and their dependencies, similarly to cargo, make, \
or Gradle.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965221995624869*^9},ExpressionUUID->"abda0caf-5b3e-4246-8a20-\
a262263e409a"],

Cell["\<\
lean type checks and compiles individual Lean files as well as providing \
information to programmer tools about files that are currently being written. \
Normally, lean is invoked by other tools rather than directly by users.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965221999325582*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5177738e-b21b-4972-8d25-\
a33c6954e3c5"],

Cell["\<\
Plugins for editors, such as Visual Studio Code or Emacs, that communicate \
with lean and present its information conveniently.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9652220048564243`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"953bb30d-21cb-4f38-9547-\
f2777318ef40"],

Cell["\<\
https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/Propositions-and-Proofs/#\
propositions-and-proofs\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965302785912423*^9},ExpressionUUID->"1b278522-678d-487d-9167-\
af0c5ca19abd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is about propositions as types ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3fbba9bd-9e3c-46f6-a765-7a826bc2fc36"],
 " which is the same thing we learned before as well! "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965302890001224*^9, 3.9653029061895437`*^9}, 
   3.965608547318961*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a8510c2f-8c69-409c-9959-\
4f1ac29c0e30"],

Cell["This is like simply typed lambda calculus", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965609494531052*^9, 
  3.9656095230847597`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0a05beb0-10fe-4abc-80a6-\
1cad4730040d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bidirectional typing", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965609312062112*^9, 
  3.965609315846455*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ded5a33a-94eb-4fd1-93f0-\
a79a43f88ec5"],

Cell["https://arxiv.org/pdf/1908.05839", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
