Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Sheaf",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", " "}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a79cb8f7-39c9-474a-b051-bef2128b0dcd"],
 "Theoretic Approach to consciousness"
}], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966767609433877*^9, 3.966767612608045*^9}, {
  3.96942745925331*^9, 3.969427471065185*^9}, {3.969429035614999*^9, 
  3.9694290404512877`*^9}, {3.96942917687421*^9, 3.969429176874497*^9}, {
  3.969430729484646*^9, 
  3.969430734626854*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"608abca9-8a15-45ed-965d-\
b1f5d5df6a1b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Our Our model model is based based on two assumptions\na) the the universe \
universe must must be interpreted as a sea of consciousness.\nb) Time is \
multi",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5c51ae0-8a7a-40d7-bd02-da06c535b45f"],
 "dimensional and non",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8a7614c-f9dc-43bd-9bff-98fa0b7817b2"],
 "linear."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969427506841281*^9, 3.969427544769865*^9}, {
  3.969427577820819*^9, 3.969427590220022*^9}, {3.9694288050981703`*^9, 
  3.969428806365861*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d1a36204-8d0c-4ccf-aa30-\
c825b7c7af9c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We consider a topological space ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["T", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cba7aca6-88d2-4628-86c2-6bf137bfbf54"],
 " of arbitrarily large dimension which we call time and consider the \
category ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9b9f8ba-d3e8-4376-a3fe-a77411ed93b5"],
 " of pre",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c104b94-8fd9-4e4c-98cf-ed8b6ca4239a"],
 "sheaves of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["T", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "dbf0fc7e-d9f8-494a-a528-d4420768b474"],
 ", which is the universe. Note that a presheaf is a contravariant functor \
from category of open sets in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["T", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b82abd5-e522-43d9-9412-3f431af15ed8"],
 " to the target category (sets/rings etc.). And a morphism of presheaves is \
just a natural transformation.  It is appropriate to think of inaminate \
objects as particularly poor presheaves. For example, a single particle in a \
stable state could be represented by a constant sheaf whose stalk is the \
trivial object in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5579419-771a-4109-a7e2-89d615a4ede6"],
 " or something like that. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96942761741451*^9, 3.969427651797577*^9}, {
   3.969427806212057*^9, 3.969427823231331*^9}, {3.9694288830049467`*^9, 
   3.969428916874085*^9}, {3.969429177838283*^9, 3.9694291933726873`*^9}, {
   3.969429236042605*^9, 3.96942925889788*^9}, {3.969429289758171*^9, 
   3.969429313134584*^9}, {3.969429571504705*^9, 3.969429577701747*^9}, 
   3.969429835215661*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4b9cabae-1570-461a-a2d8-\
4dc649b66813"],

Cell["\<\
A brain can be represetned by some interesting presheaf. A thought can be a \
section of the brain. And now we transition fo the next paper. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969429836855627*^9, 3.969429868992247*^9}, {
  3.969429987627529*^9, 3.969429996832438*^9}, {3.969529131457366*^9, 
  3.9695291315447397`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf0c4b38-f31a-4b79-81cb-\
166d46c7c60d"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["An integrated brain function (Kato, Nishimura)", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9694299983540087`*^9, 3.9694300012912493`*^9}, {
  3.9695253708124847`*^9, 
  3.969525375061064*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"16c0b1c7-63a6-415e-886f-\
59ba9a09d6e3"],

Cell["AlgebraicDynamics@42", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9694313246354933`*^9, 
  3.969431328929656*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"56ae0c94-4033-4c60-9201-\
f9532634d8da"],

Cell["\<\
Note that sheaves give way to translate local information into global \
information. Because if we have an object defined on different local regions \
which agree on their intersection, it corresponds to a unique global object \
of which is is part. Maybe our thoughts are local but they are glued together \
and go into the subconsciousness (sheafification).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969430002642054*^9, 3.969430054833387*^9}, {
  3.9694307458771677`*^9, 
  3.969430773679764*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d57179a-a678-47ee-89e1-\
fe1a79c7beef"],

Cell["\<\
These are researches started in the computer science department at Oxford. \
Abrmasky, emeritus professor, studies a unified model of various theories \
from quantum physics to natural environments. Prof. Bob Coecke and Pulman \
also study in connection to artificial intelligence, linguistics, and \
cognitive science.  They show how the same mathematical structures arise in \
various areas of classical computation and use string diagrams derived from \
quantum mechanics to gain insights into the nature of natural language [15].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969431072572311*^9, 3.9694311468889513`*^9}, {
  3.96943119411545*^9, 
  3.969431236474069*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"629381bf-cb4a-4577-8fd7-\
cd33dfd99cff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Topos). A topos is the category of sheaves over a category with a \
grothendiek topology, called a site."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969431401954134*^9, 3.969431424989128*^9}, {
  3.969431483646204*^9, 
  3.969431488604075*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f0f2b7e9-77e1-47d0-99c9-\
495a74ae3981"],

Cell["\<\
Applications to physics, especially for foundations of quantum theory and \
quantum gravity, were initiated by the topos theoretic school at imperial \
college led by C.Isham.  Our project on the formulations of the thinking \
processes began with the results in Kato-Nishimura [20] for
two types of grasping concepts, and Kato-Nishimura [21] for thought \
processes. In this paper, we will intepret brain imaging results as a \
transition from local to global information in terms of sheaf theoretic \
methods.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969431532889684*^9, 3.96943156686679*^9}, {
  3.969432159063881*^9, 3.96943215920905*^9}, {3.969434681444794*^9, 
  3.969434681716235*^9}, {3.9695244321432753`*^9, 3.969524432257497*^9}, {
  3.9695254254856*^9, 3.9695254285118637`*^9}, {3.969525531871282*^9, 
  3.969525579942954*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2f7cede4-6eaf-481c-a0c2-\
71324cdd2c9a"],

Cell["Well, I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t quite understand this over here very \
well.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969529051139786*^9, 
  3.969529060554523*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d1f2ba9c-4313-4b7c-baa7-\
197c91fab918"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["AI agents ", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965817027737589*^9, 
  3.965817029441595*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7fcc0fe8-0de7-41df-9763-\
599c074c108d"],

Cell["Idea is that it learns by itself. ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965817031251186*^9, 3.965817036695451*^9}, {
  3.966572460336278*^9, 
  3.966572462378087*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d4e58f7d-1377-4598-b29a-\
b02301ab9645"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Neural networks and physical systems with emergent collective computational \
abilities\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966896722223553*^9, 3.966896732531123*^9}, {
  3.966896788287944*^9, 
  3.966896793842556*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a6b3d293-2915-4e70-ac74-\
391de590fc47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There are classes of physical systems whose spontaneous be-havior can be \
used as a form of general (and error-correcting) content-addressable memory. \
Consider the time evolution of a physical system that can be described by a \
set of general co-ordinates. A point in state space then represents the \
instantaneous condition of the system. Equations of motion of the system \
describe a flow in state space. Various classes of flow patterns are \
possible,",
 StyleBox[" but the systems of use for memory particularly include those that \
flow to-ward locally stable points from anywhere within regions around those \
points",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". ",
 "This is analagous to error correction."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966899092378*^9, 
  3.966899226398782*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed995c3b-b210-4f88-86ed-\
e208d937dc8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Basically, if we have a physical system with limit points ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["X", "a"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d32c2d9a-947d-4e45-be6e-51331a8c419a"],
 " (where these are state vectors). So here if the system starts near any of \
these i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["X", 
      RowBox[{"a", " "}]], " ", "+", " ", "\[CapitalDelta]"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "5957e79b-d373-48dd-8aac-aaf5130ae053"],
 ", then it will end up at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["X", 
    RowBox[{"a", " "}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd2eba88-bc0c-4250-83f6-a7369a49ab83"],
 ". Here, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["X", 
      RowBox[{"a", " "}]], " ", "+", " ", "\[CapitalDelta]"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc990d8-5ef1-4b12-b703-a3ac0a5a9ce9"],
 " can be thought of as having partial knowledge of a system, and then it \
converges towards ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["X", 
    RowBox[{"a", " "}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "81711a5b-9874-4e19-b5cc-47318b7bf1ec"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9668990989048347`*^9, 3.966899113125091*^9}, {
  3.9668992279819717`*^9, 3.9668992341776953`*^9}, {3.9668994779943657`*^9, 
  3.966899542060933*^9}, {3.966899598887055*^9, 3.966899622596171*^9}, {
  3.966899731997798*^9, 
  3.9668997385833473`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"417749a5-d7d7-42b3-9e7f-\
104e8f44fcd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each neuron has a potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "i"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1350979-1fc2-4725-8dd1-b39d0bc973dc"],
 " which is either 0 (not firing) and 1 (firing at max rate). The strength of \
a connection between neuron ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d19c131a-a534-4096-88a5-bdb53721ba76"],
 " to neuron ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "624f660a-3ffa-4ac2-bdcc-f3406545ccbd"],
 " is defined as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["T", "ij"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6c161c4-f269-4f0b-95bb-e9b0005b1220"],
 ". Each neuron has a threshold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "i"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a77bac-ba00-4fa0-ab05-80b1a9e35bab"],
 ". If ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{"j", "\[NotEqual]", "i"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["T", "ij"], 
      SubscriptBox["V", "j"]}]}], ">", 
    SubscriptBox["U", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9b1430-ff7c-4246-8771-5b264422a342"],
 ", then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["V", "i"], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0135e46f-b65b-4352-bfa5-d2ff104dea51"],
 " and if not, it goes to 0. This captures the intuition that if the \
surrounding neurons of a neuron are firing, then the neuron also starts \
firing. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966900003537915*^9, 3.9669000552298317`*^9}, {
   3.966900085861496*^9, 3.966900198556941*^9}, 
   3.96690740302942*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ff9a1459-e72d-4f31-92c7-\
4a455296a84f"],

Cell["The information storage algorithm", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9669000474578753`*^9, 3.9669000483249207`*^9}, {
  3.9669002808246717`*^9, 
  3.966900287387228*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6127e8f4-1157-47d8-b881-\
ae16a1182eb9"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Compositional framework for markov processes", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96848658706607*^9, 
  3.9684865948057823`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f1a87e6f-b515-4706-9392-\
91c29aa5c678"],

Cell["\<\
All of this somehow helps one understand open systems in some way.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96849559742242*^9, 
  3.968495607191818*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c4c276b5-f1f0-4ba7-902e-\
51c085174a2f"],

Cell["\<\
A continuous-time Markov chain is a way to specify the dynamics of a population
which is spread across some finite set of states. Population can flow between
the states. The larger the population of a state, the more rapidly population
flows out of the state.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968492228147952*^9, 3.968492228825417*^9}, {
  3.9684924643016376`*^9, 
  3.968492471476747*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0964e708-404a-4297-b337-\
f83625c12d4c"],

Cell["\<\
Because of this property, under certain conditions the populations of the \
states are in some equilibrium.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968492504982813*^9, 
  3.968492527916943*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e3f44c31-d507-417c-87d9-\
c762c52eff43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Okay, there is some interesting paper about how block",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8faa455a-3c63-4bc1-8736-6051a588cb25"],
 "boxing something is compositional for circuits. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9684925874450502`*^9, 
  3.96849264892835*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9d3c2768-f1fd-40a9-b395-\
8aed0ed9afcc"],

Cell["\<\
At least since the work of Prigogine [9, 20], it is widely accepted that a \
large
class of systems minimize entropy production in a nonequilibrium steady \
state. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968492699601687*^9, 
  3.9684927017292213`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"eb07990e-dd2e-49ea-9d20-\
84f168adbcb2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

