      "], "RGB", "XYZ"], Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|"XMP" -> <||>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{679., 224.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 679.}, {0, 224.}}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968494375088415*^9, 
  3.9684943803766317`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a42ff526-122a-41ee-9ca1-\
571b671d6f91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t this some sort of a multicategory? Well, here \
this is a morphism between 2 objects, the input object consisting of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]6 and 1/2\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], and the output \
object consisting of a 2. If we describe DetBalMark, we see that this forms a \
dagger compact category, an then we can get operations between 2 Markov \
processes. We can tensor 2 morphisms together using the bifunctor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[TensorProduct]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "44cb6e91-4c70-4277-ae58-18789f98d0e5"],
 " and we get another Markov process. Dagger compact categories are a well",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a62eb9e5-4a09-41b5-8693-af0d600b85bd"],
 "known framework to describe systems with inputs and outputs."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968494678935135*^9, 3.968494756263969*^9}, {
  3.968494811123013*^9, 3.968494811977963*^9}, {3.968495038274824*^9, 
  3.968495055547248*^9}, {3.968495306038986*^9, 3.9684953273871717`*^9}, {
  3.9684953913559227`*^9, 
  3.968495434604836*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"09b896af-6d47-47c9-b2b1-\
cbf4909f8a33"],

Cell["\<\
There\[CloseCurlyQuote]s also the theory of decorated cospans which is useful \
to describe what an open system actually is and how we can comprehend that. \
It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a useful formalism, but one wonders about how useful it \
is for making an applied project.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968495897211256*^9, 3.9684959097303*^9}, {
  3.968496284086955*^9, 3.9684962962415953`*^9}, {3.968496405061318*^9, 
  3.9684964199028*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f106c0b5-6611-4f0a-a387-a232965cad8a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Syntax/Semantics", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968571538397274*^9, 
  3.96857154640165*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8cc443fd-83cf-4d89-a8c2-\
acbb43eff86e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Making sense of sensory input", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968584147669612*^9, 
  3.968584156122276*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c5e1945b-036f-4628-9f30-\
22506eac148b"],

Cell["\<\
Here we attempt to answer the question: what does it mean to make sense of a \
sensory sequence, which is often unlabelled? This is a useful conceptual \
study because as humans, we receive sensory input all the time and we can \
somehow figure out these \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]patterns\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that help.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968584471895049*^9, 3.968584523780235*^9}, {
  3.968584661327697*^9, 3.968584676957652*^9}, {3.968585146391699*^9, 
  3.9685851482781553`*^9}, {3.968585355712031*^9, 
  3.968585355898323*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bd778fc9-6ecc-41a0-be8d-\
0cff4f469058"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One approach is to treat the sensory sequence as the ",
 StyleBox["input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to a",
 StyleBox[" supervised learning problem.",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " Given a sequence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", 
    RowBox[{"1", ":", "t"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e8c16669-4407-4207-ae91-c5d986870636"],
 " of sensory data from time steps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "386c1173-c794-4468-b312-1f727a640a45"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "065f3140-0f66-401d-a93c-9858d29e2acd"],
 ", we want to make a prob. distribution law which maximises ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["x", 
      RowBox[{"t", "+", "1"}]], "|", 
     SubscriptBox["x", "t"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "58f3457e-b065-4a82-b39c-05a5b6700e72"],
 ". We can also train it to retredict past sensory readings."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968585181631864*^9, 3.96858530104537*^9}, {
  3.968585343782987*^9, 
  3.9685853469549527`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"04449773-698c-4eca-858e-\
462757261bea"],

Cell["\<\
In this paper, we try to formalize what is a mental model of the input \
received, which gives rise to these sensory readings. In our mind, we seem to \
develop some sort of a causal structure: like this thing causes this other \
thing or some sort of a relation which may not be defined. And the mental \
model becomes more and more stable if the structure becomes more consistent \
and clearer! (maybe the unfinished \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]dangling edges\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are given higher priority). \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96858540732268*^9, 3.968585412010254*^9}, {
  3.968585595591469*^9, 3.968585698412145*^9}, {3.968585974475895*^9, 
  3.968585995131949*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"09acc8b7-1d50-4c95-b137-\
ef52157c927f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We think that: making sense of the sensory data ",
 StyleBox["requires",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " some underlying reality with hypothetical concetps lying in some abstract \
space that gives rise. Basically, some theory, which is built on foundational \
structure like causality and relation. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968585720888537*^9, 3.9685857584227066`*^9}, {
  3.968585908996624*^9, 3.968585955516299*^9}, {3.9685860629976892`*^9, 
  3.968586064053359*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7e045c0b-fd0f-49dc-9c08-\
dd7573b113cb"],

Cell["\<\
Computer agents endowed with mental models have shown to be able to achieve \
impressive performance in a variety of domains. Now, we want to build a model \
that explains a sensory sequence. One question: what form should the model \
take? We use the hidden Markov model framework which can describe sequential \
processes. A markov chain is quite easy to understand where things just \
determine on the previous step, and mostly we consider homogeneous markov \
chains.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968642333738708*^9, 3.96864234136543*^9}, {
  3.968642502930854*^9, 3.96864256054702*^9}, {3.968642609464385*^9, 
  3.968642625069444*^9}, {3.9686426885569987`*^9, 3.968642697122235*^9}, {
  3.968642759519693*^9, 3.968642770188049*^9}, {3.968751269351203*^9, 
  3.968751307940692*^9}, {3.9688414654193773`*^9, 
  3.968841466216962*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ffeac79-1073-49bc-bb27-\
2e5ad59e78b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In a hidden markov mordel, there is another flow of inforamtion that takes \
place. We have these latent states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "35a5d3bd-62d6-4323-9ce9-6204e6345f06"],
 " which change according to a Markov chain i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b51cfdca-9f9a-4467-bd94-5af9959f7c9c"],
 " is a value that is taken by the random variable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Z", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "230a3238-f020-480c-be6f-5cc9ae4da4da"],
 " in that instance. Then, the observations are a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "fcda41c6-94c0-4c5e-b69d-e50b492598c2"],
 ", which only depend on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb018f4b-c1dd-4fe1-b670-0b4dfce40db9"],
 ". Thus, there is an extra step in processing and we only see the \
observations."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9687535517839203`*^9, 
  3.968753668260273*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"83a41512-97c7-4706-9ee8-\
4d4f634ca733"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So here, we have three distinct features from other \
people\[CloseCurlyQuote]s work on receiving sensory input and getting fomr \
patterns out of them. In neural net approaches, the posited theory of \
evolution i.e. the state transitions is not human readable b/c it is just a \
neural net. But we work with a language to explain thos langauge transitions. \
Also, here, we address that there is a hidden layer and actually associate \
that layer with different type signature. So we have different types for them \
and deal with them separately. Also, the state representation is human",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbb6f9e1-d186-4270-9dc3-093c52d4c0de"],
 "readable and symbolic. (idk what that means). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754037368435*^9, 3.9687540782310143`*^9}, {
  3.968754153309763*^9, 3.968754198837061*^9}, {3.968754352437419*^9, 
  3.9687543910052013`*^9}, {3.96875442420087*^9, 
  3.96875444187272*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0be31f5d-ab89-47e9-9d8f-\
224abd4d9f4e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Function free atom). A function free atom is an expression of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["t", "1"], ",", "...", ",", 
     SubscriptBox["t", "n"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c9f97a4-266e-45ea-be80-400db748ce77"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "44adc550-2146-4f88-9598-492da0f9e77f"],
 " is a predicate of arity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"n", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "81f08fef-6a54-43b0-a303-d4dd997e66f4"],
 " and each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["t", "i"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "313920f9-0470-412c-acba-b8396eea02a0"],
 " is either a variable or a constant. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754903319944*^9, 
  3.968754903322115*^9}, {3.968755509544385*^9, 
  3.968755509546133*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e2678bd3-9b6a-40fb-9aaf-\
9de832cb248b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here we use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", 
    RowBox[{"c", "..."}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "86fca070-19db-4d11-9211-ba8cfd9d330d"],
 " for constants and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"X", ",", "Y", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Z", ".."}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1513e092-bac4-4342-9d03-427cb8bc63c5"],
 " for variables. We can also define a substitution as a mapping "
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754903319944*^9, 
  3.968754903322115*^9}, {3.968755510233128*^9, 3.968755517182666*^9}, {
  3.968886399536727*^9, 3.968886399539711*^9}, {3.9688864359657183`*^9, 
  3.968886448106111*^9}, {3.9688867788850317`*^9, 
  3.9688868327725353`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f48e93ee-fef9-4a4f-948f-\
8e82535368fe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Substitution). A substitution is a mapping from variables to terms."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754903319944*^9, 
  3.968754903322115*^9}, {3.968755510233128*^9, 3.968755517182666*^9}, {
  3.968886399536727*^9, 3.968886399539711*^9}, {3.9688864359657183`*^9, 
  3.968886448106111*^9}, {3.9688867788850317`*^9, 
  3.968886853802588*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"020e78aa-90e2-4c45-9d38-\
ab98be858d38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Ground atom). A ground atom is a logical atom that contains no \
variables."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754903319944*^9, 
  3.968754903322115*^9}, {3.968755510233128*^9, 3.968755517182666*^9}, {
  3.968886400362822*^9, 
  3.968886419013592*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6162fe3a-b25f-4f7f-b44e-\
4e0fae960d50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Datalog clause). A",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "datalog clause is a definite clause of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], "\[And]"}], "..."}], "\[And]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "n"]}], " ", "->", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "0"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e942c0e9-bffa-47c7-a541-352c6fbc373d"],
 " where each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "i"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb6cf06a-530a-4365-84fa-ff9dd107bbff"],
 " is a function free atom and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"n", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c109278-4b39-453a-97ae-46117bcc6edc"],
 ". And a datalog program is a set of datalog clauses."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.9687551812931547`*^9, 3.968755181296994*^9}, {
  3.96875542115*^9, 3.9687554349748774`*^9}, {3.9687555223862553`*^9, 
  3.968755523993334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2b450fa3-d480-43fb-8071-\
d94d5978ba8e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Literal). A literal is an atom ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Alpha]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "02ad0453-cd1f-4d1f-a55d-31f650410405"],
 " or a negated atom ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"not", " ", "\[Alpha]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8132fa0b-7dbe-40b2-ab32-b1f79e701ef1"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.968755181835058*^9, 3.96875520144816*^9}, {
  3.9687555190432796`*^9, 
  3.96875551904482*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d7c0e2d-7044-4f4a-91df-\
49b8dc22dbdc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Normal logic program). A normal logic program is a  set of clauses of the \
form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "0"], " ", "\[LeftArrow]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"]}], ",", "...", ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "n"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d708372-c3d8-40a3-a8d8-372ae4a19616"],
 " where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "0"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f4932d5-b902-4b0b-b379-d9b1e785e913"],
 " is an atom, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], ",", "...", ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "n"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b3521cee-af39-47f5-b312-f61e18268afe"],
 " is a conjunction of literals and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"n", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bd4c140-279f-49ca-a76e-ca521bec83cf"],
 ". "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.968755181835058*^9, 3.96875520144816*^9}, {
  3.968755519602854*^9, 3.968755594009282*^9}, {3.968755668275256*^9, 
  3.968755668470071*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e6ce9e0b-8faf-45d3-abec-\
c567bbb3ce57"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here, we are describing the input to the sensory sequence in the form of \
ground atoms of first order logic; so a sensory reading featuring sensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fd8f2432-0091-4280-b55f-e982d6d09c2d"],
 " can be represented by a ground atom ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "(", "a", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d037976d-cd36-4dba-9988-a99bf4d61f9e"],
 " for predicate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3d3395e9-2d9f-48b4-b95e-a7ad369943f4"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968755625617879*^9, 3.968755686182391*^9}, {
  3.968841648758956*^9, 3.9688416579009132`*^9}, {3.968841740795687*^9, 
  3.96884174489331*^9}, {3.968886260484694*^9, 
  3.9688862624430017`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"19302ea4-3356-476d-ae76-\
98c305a91c8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Unambigous symbolic sensory sequence). An unambigous symbolic sensory \
sequence",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "is a sequence of sets of ground atoms i.e. a sequence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["S", "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox["S", "2"], ",", "..."}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b95f020b-a17e-4327-b5dc-271765605a94"],
 ", where every ",
 "state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "t"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "df70c872-6e91-49d6-9b46-e5e2124bea0b"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["S", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5b98d3d3-0e04-4b43-a68e-60115c96d846"],
 " is a set of ground atoms, representing a ",
 "partial description of the world at a discrete time step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "56e9a087-0c4f-4228-92c0-b10d56cb5f25"],
 ". An atom ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"p", "(", "a", ")"}], "\[Element]", 
    SubscriptBox["S", "t"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "69858a35-3f7f-45a7-9cf6-1eb458009d61"],
 " represents that sensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0554dc6c-3430-44e4-9f29-8cb13ca91845"],
 " has property ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ff7f7d10-199f-4340-9c49-6bc503264036"],
 " at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "94760550-6e8b-4d38-a420-e18f9cb0a580"],
 ". An atom ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"r", "(", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], ")"}], "\[Element]", 
    SubscriptBox["S", "t"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a8fe34ec-ec63-49ea-b626-973b4242b515"],
 " represents that sensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b85de0c5-638b-4b9b-bf4c-225f9846a427"],
 " is related via relation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["r", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1fc1c1cf-d080-4316-9b22-22c88972d345"],
 " to value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["b", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bbc0b1ef-0510-4297-81da-ad24c655f027"],
 " at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "77ad8904-31f7-4038-9cb9-69dbda760c2b"],
 ". "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.968755181835058*^9, 3.96875520144816*^9}, {
  3.968755519602854*^9, 3.968755623278988*^9}, {3.96888626360085*^9, 
  3.968886287855734*^9}, {3.96888761555738*^9, 3.968887783475514*^9}, {
  3.968887891259369*^9, 
  3.968887891262553*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f3847633-fbcf-4cad-b788-\
b72b4198e59b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Theory). A theory is a four",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ff0f144-de12-4f1c-ad83-4aaa3a550c29"],
 "tuple ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", ",", "I", ",", "R", ",", "C"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "dac9a61e-1ad6-4295-aaf4-a1fa8aed05aa"],
 " of Datalog elements where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Phi]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cf15193-d0a2-4328-9d4b-8e5997c04a94"],
 " is a type signature, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["I", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fcc5532-152b-4edc-97c0-b43efbc1253e"],
 " is set of initial conditions, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["R", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "554479e1-cd3a-4517-bdab-839524eb6e16"],
 " is a set of rules describing the dynamics, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "a03c25f0-2865-4fde-be3f-d70db42e7b94"],
 " is a set of constraints."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.968755181835058*^9, 3.96875520144816*^9}, {
  3.968755519602854*^9, 3.968755623278988*^9}, {3.96888626360085*^9, 
  3.968886287855734*^9}, {3.9688876155573797`*^9, 3.968887783475514*^9}, {
  3.96888789209138*^9, 3.968887931614056*^9}, {3.9688880119169703`*^9, 
  3.968888032213307*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dad0f8f6-d03c-48e8-b707-\
c866d29f7ecc"],

Cell["", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968754414443924*^9, 3.968754422309228*^9}, {
  3.968754685594479*^9, 3.968754752858816*^9}, {3.968754904203457*^9, 
  3.968754956101078*^9}, {3.968755181835058*^9, 3.96875520144816*^9}, {
  3.968755519602854*^9, 3.968755623278988*^9}, {3.96888626360085*^9, 
  3.968886287855734*^9}, {3.9688876155573797`*^9, 3.968887783475514*^9}, {
  3.96888789209138*^9, 3.968887931614056*^9}, {3.9688880119169703`*^9, 
  3.9688880282444057`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac5f7070-abea-4883-b2da-\
45c05adcbaf8"],

Cell["Ok. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come back to this.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9688882184424343`*^9, 
  3.9688882235396023`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"89eaf3bb-26ff-4675-bdd5-\
360ceb713628"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Relation", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968642251685422*^9, 
  3.968642254057735*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6e206bfc-52b4-4d48-9895-\
61f95a2ffbd5"],

Cell["\<\
This is very relevant to make an AI Proof engine because here the sensory \
input can be thought of as some exploration of the metamathematical space. \
Now, that exploration will be driven by intuition and other things, and so \
given this input data, the AI can learn how to make sense of it by building a \
metnal model inside it. And the reason why mental models tend to be \
relational or causal because they imply some sort of data processing, which \
is designed to reduce entropy (data processing inequality). Reducing entropy \
means that we can make some predictions. Of course, this is really vague, but \
intuitively makes sense.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968586061057004*^9, 3.968586067087789*^9}, {
  3.968586248242852*^9, 3.968586312008175*^9}, {3.968586477869128*^9, 
  3.968586515680465*^9}, {3.9686419628642*^9, 3.968641987604944*^9}, {
  3.96864216343279*^9, 3.9686421724105587`*^9}, {3.9688417062740297`*^9, 
  3.968841710272429*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7effc2e6-92df-4c57-bf3c-\
b1d4ccffcca4"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Making sense of raw input", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9685745104170103`*^9, 3.968574515299224*^9}, {
  3.968579978476169*^9, 
  3.968579978979423*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"128bf6b9-4b61-4da2-aac8-\
99c07ed38bdf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There are 2 approaches of ",
 StyleBox["interpreting the results of ML systems. ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "One is that we have an ML system which is already trained and we are trying \
to understand its inner state based on what it is doing. The other approach \
is that we constrain the design of the ML system that its results can be \
interpreted easily."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968575110859913*^9, 3.968575126585547*^9}, {
  3.9685752377475157`*^9, 3.9685753063202457`*^9}, {3.96857991453295*^9, 
  3.968579917557423*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c760ebb2-f588-428c-9b39-\
7c10e9db46c1"],

Cell["\<\
In this paper: they have taken the second approach to unsupervised learning. \
Here, the system takes an input as a temporal sequence of raw unprocessed \
information and interpretable theory capturing the regularities in that \
sequence. So we build a unsupervised machine learning algorithm (so there\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s no input output over here) which builds first order \
theories and a neural net that takes the raw input and transforms into some \
symbolic information.  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968575335559637*^9, 3.96857547847733*^9}, {
   3.968575588475133*^9, 3.9685756099442*^9}, {3.968581573821769*^9, 
   3.968581621012154*^9}, 
   3.96858266325891*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a5df1262-f3fc-4347-8933-\
f3f2cfa5329d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So unsupervised learning is a field of machine learning where we make sense \
of unlabelled data. Obviously, this problem is not well",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "77eb11bc-14be-471c-bcab-91535863478f"],
 "defined. What does \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]making sense\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] mean over here? It probably means that there is some \
pattern or higher order structure. In other words, the unlabelled data set \
doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t display complete randomness \[Implies] i.e. the \
output random variable has entropy less than the uniform distribution. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968583418968212*^9, 3.968583421040032*^9}, {
  3.968583599212357*^9, 3.968583637185113*^9}, {3.968583805835528*^9, 
  3.968583877037746*^9}, {3.968584058077097*^9, 
  3.968584071940744*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d3602073-d4e2-4808-aa89-\
a93dfe61f251"],

Cell["T", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.968586058808958*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4b048dff-52a8-4728-8894-\
723f248684a3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"1.6", "*", "70"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968575190743384*^9, 3.968575192262828*^9}},
