Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Graph embedding", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969037728129898*^9, 
  3.969037730728611*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"75c9cdaa-3365-4bef-93c5-\
cd3b00b5b577"],

Cell["\<\
This can be an interesting project here I guess. Exploring the \
metamathematical structure with a lot of python code and stuff. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969360359168857*^9, 3.969360369600456*^9}, {
  3.969360404053409*^9, 3.969360414969502*^9}, {3.9694545364230537`*^9, 
  3.969454555982041*^9}, {3.9694547544171*^9, 
  3.969454756629692*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8872d2bc-365b-4ef2-9e8e-\
e464df1c02f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come up with some sort of a model. So let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s say that we learn a concept of a set and and say that it \
is a collection of objects. Then we can represent this in some sort of a \
graph with node labelled ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["Set", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a25c64a2-32da-4831-9787-737c9d7819a8"],
 " and it being a collection of objects. So it is linked with the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]idea\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of a collection of \
objects perhaps by undirected edges. Then we have the directed edges to \
examples such as the naturals etc. For instance, something like this:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9693595455556498`*^9, 3.969359558499096*^9}, {
  3.969359589226268*^9, 3.969359686449671*^9}, {3.969359817261242*^9, 
  3.969359819439829*^9}, {3.969359857129225*^9, 3.9693599496652117`*^9}, {
  3.969360170253515*^9, 3.969360176180282*^9}, {3.96936033410769*^9, 
  3.969360334920335*^9}, {3.969361144508442*^9, 
  3.9693611481988792`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4f67696c-6616-4bbb-8ec5-\
0e1c8dc8dd5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now, we read the definition of equality of sets that 2 sets are equal when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[ForAll]", "x"}], ")"}], "x"}], "\[Element]", " ", "A"}], 
    " ", "\[Equivalent]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"x", "\[Element]", " ", "B"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "99ec314a-8503-4a6a-8a6d-9978e0785a2b"],
 ". How will this embed into our representation? We have 2 options, broadly \
speaking. One option is that we explicitly compress the information by \
creating a data structure that physically operates in that way. Or the second \
option is that we use a somewhat normal embedding and use the fact that the \
existence of patterns  \[Implies] the neural net will figure out the function."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969445856398196*^9, 3.96944592756671*^9}, {
   3.96944601558067*^9, 3.969446055702832*^9}, {3.969454264794424*^9, 
   3.969454266249457*^9}, {3.969454601768494*^9, 3.969454612125361*^9}, 
   3.969454648373416*^9, {3.969454767224639*^9, 3.969454840824792*^9}, {
   3.969454917201999*^9, 3.969454920613777*^9}, {3.969455376745862*^9, 
   3.969455424469146*^9}, {3.969455461031564*^9, 3.969455533447215*^9}, {
   3.969455665543395*^9, 3.969455687670529*^9}, {3.969455725095996*^9, 
   3.969455764280514*^9}, {3.969455862160493*^9, 3.969455908083035*^9}, {
   3.96945634069305*^9, 3.9694563747918167`*^9}, {3.969456414032891*^9, 
   3.9694564926662602`*^9}, {3.969456700209062*^9, 3.969456767692661*^9}, 
   3.96945688924461*^9, {3.969458000438846*^9, 3.9694580148224363`*^9}, {
   3.969458078457542*^9, 3.969458114468518*^9}, {3.96945872797234*^9, 
   3.9694587396585407`*^9}, {3.969458793970475*^9, 3.969458956878587*^9}, {
   3.9694590213441*^9, 
   3.969459036616997*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2c69e3f0-8ec4-4bc2-bac0-\
2a771358f68a"],

Cell["Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try the second option.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969459043481056*^9, 
  3.969459048045747*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e3fcd2bb-2134-4359-960c-\
f132785c4cd5"],

Cell["\<\
Like some sort of a compression algorithm that reduces hte information. or \
something...like smaller....hmmmmmm. i dont know..some sort of a compression. \
But doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t the compression happen in the processing stage? \
Maybe. Who knows. Note that the existence of those patterns implies that \
thing over here.... yeah. .aybe. who knows. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s see how \
that works. 



Well, it seems like that the brain or the engine can somehow categorize the \
information to understand how to deal with examples/etc. It is somewhat of a \
thinking framework which is really weird. The only problem I see right now is \
the explicit task of doing the prediction, which is why i proposed the \
somewhat superposition of the conscious and the subconscious mind. It seems \
that the act of solving problems itself teaches the AI something, so maybe \
the distinction isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t between learning and doing. The \
subconscious might just be an arrangement of knowlefsqdge and the conscious \
might just be an action on the space in some way...but that action changes \
the spacet i the subscionsious in some wya.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969459036009853*^9, 3.9694590395399933`*^9}, {
  3.969459143143022*^9, 3.9694591521374607`*^9}, {3.970998341176112*^9, 
