1035791abef2"],

Cell["\<\
Now the agent reads the description of the equality of sets. How does this \
information embed in the subconscious? It seems that it just floats around; \
however, there must be something that happens. Instead of thinking of them as \
chunks of data, they might be some sort of perturbations. For instance, the \
thought itself is an open set of some sort of a sheaf or something. I don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know. Rrading something like this will be useful.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969424139068122*^9, 3.9694241490896797`*^9}, {
  3.9694251000926037`*^9, 3.9694251386620827`*^9}, {3.969425217354846*^9, 
