Cell["Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s assume this distinction for now. ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9693634141393137`*^9, 3.969363420044454*^9}, {
  3.969364088600786*^9, 
  3.969364089517138*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a0b956be-dd0b-4431-a535-\
3d50e6683bed"],

Cell["\<\
Now that the input layer is lean, the question is how to embed this in a sort \
of object that changes dynamically with time. Here, we are assuming that \
there is a structure of knowledge that acts like a memory of what the AI \
agent knows. And from that structure, understanding and intelligence is an \
emergent process. For instance, in the case of Chat GPT, the input data is \
the text and the embedding is in the form of tokens. So there is a discrete \
unit. In the case of lean data, we can think of a hypergraph as an embedding. \
The thing is that then the output will be a function on the hypergraph. Well, \
let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try! I think that this is pretty interesting. Yeah. I \
will grind this shit out. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969037733055033*^9, 3.969037740298925*^9}, {
  3.969037863764603*^9, 3.969038075571946*^9}, {3.969038122423436*^9, 
