Cell[TextData[{
 "Symbolically, I can define this as a set over here as raw input. Howwever, \
there is some sort of a weird understanding happenign with the word \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]such that\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]where i say ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e26d9ce4-57f5-4369-9612-6a98d3a29c31"],
 "such that ...it seems that imm choosing thos enumbers...it is something \
very vague in my head which ic an\[CloseCurlyQuote]t explain...this weird \
inutition...act ofn choosing. And this is thing is useful to undersstand \
here.having a discrete structure seems difficult. maybe we can have a richer \
structure., Like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", "n"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a4bcdd-ed85-4724-8022-6542fbd468c8"],
 " or some other sheaf theoretic ideas captursing differen thigns. Hmm. This \
is kind of crazy over ehre. . How to do this> Seems like there is some \
automatic procedure that does somehting"
}], "Item",
