Cell["\<\
The thing is that information only exists on a relational level. So I\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]m trying to understand that if we have the real numbers, \
then can we quantify or just have  a framework for understanding how much \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]information\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] can we stoee over \
the real numbers For instance, if we have a system of raw input or raw real \
world data, and we labelled each instance with a real number, then how much \
relational information we will be able to store? This is a good question; \
however, a bit hard to understand. I think it may have to do with predicting \
input output. I wish there was a good framework to understand this. We can \
start developing such a frameowrk. Hmm.\
\>", "Item",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
