Cell["\<\
Define what a set is. On an abstract level, the AI\[CloseCurlyQuote]s state \
is a continuous thing that changes. in the case of neural nets. there is per \
token it updates in some way or in some sort of a discrete time step. We can \
do that over here in a discrete setting. where we feed it a definition or an \
example r something followed by some continuous processing. First, the idea \
is that of an embedding. And the usage of using reals is that if there us a \
pattern, there must exist some embedding which is learned by the net such \
that an input output relationship is there. Okay. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
start building this thing. --\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968913615331462*^9, 3.96891362066566*^9}, {
   3.968924480845211*^9, 3.968924539060829*^9}, {3.968924574247414*^9, 
   3.968924600916236*^9}, {3.968924680050566*^9, 3.968924692856223*^9}, {
   3.968924885725226*^9, 3.968924888235184*^9}, {3.968926562795502*^9, 
   3.968926565541776*^9}, 3.968926843583131*^9, {3.968926985533264*^9, 
   3.968926985733582*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"752f9954-2c31-47bd-94dd-\
b48df3e67df7"],

Cell["\<\
Then, it is a collection of sets...to get that intuition..how? Examples. But \
what presentation idea...or somthing...indont know...hmmmm.....knowledge \
base...i dont know....well,,,,id ont need to. example. pack...ntotation. \
Well, this is what it is.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968913622048197*^9, 3.968913653116924*^9}, {
  3.9689136958770657`*^9, 3.968913745627173*^9}, {3.96892317847466*^9, 
  3.96892320221715*^9}, {3.969454673723946*^9, 
  3.9694546769468107`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"64f4a63e-7d56-439e-a75e-\
cecf7d6a0d65"],

Cell["2. ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968912128290662*^9, 
  3.968912128505319*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b9c8bf70-642e-49e3-b805-\
ca7be3485795"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. Representation layer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "afcabcda-fca3-4682-ab62-090565954dd4"],
 " here, the mathematical notation is represented by some object that can be \
taken in by the AI. In the case of humans, it i just written in english or it \
is represented by some visual understanding. Now, it seems that the \
representation is relevant to the intuition itself, which is about finding \
the patterns and regularities, higher order structure,  etc. In chat gpt, the \
AI understands natural language because the input is literally a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]string data type\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] over here. \
And then it decomposes into tokens and stuff.  In HUMANS, the inputt is the \
senses, mainly vision and sound. ANd who knows how complex image processing \
actually is. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s maybe using very sophisticated physical \
processes to model all these things."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968572846270807*^9, 3.968572873448983*^9}, {
  3.968572976110895*^9, 3.968572990637046*^9}, {3.9685731084647083`*^9, 
  3.968573159485563*^9}, {3.968573507162107*^9, 3.968573552606097*^9}, {
  3.968573698792926*^9, 3.9685737087555323`*^9}, {3.968573739461277*^9, 
  3.968573775098075*^9}, {3.968574317448188*^9, 3.968574339672936*^9}, {
  3.968888833960676*^9, 3.968888846314893*^9}, {3.968910095710972*^9, 
  3.9689101235763493`*^9}, {3.968910167886462*^9, 
  3.968910183449584*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4c19ba7f-da41-40c5-82e0-\
f1e474f172c3"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Teach Logic", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968212135374867*^9, 3.968212136156988*^9}, {
  3.968212222831189*^9, 
  3.9682122266949873`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e20aefa6-0c98-41d3-8a71-\
6646d9d46c52"],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to make some implementations. On the outset, I \
think that a compositional setting is valid where we can make a very simple \
AI which is compatible with whatever it learns later. Maybe the intelligence \
is somewhat of an emergent phenomenon of learning very basic things composed \
together and the effect is exponential so we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t really \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]expect it\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. Maybe. Seems legit.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968565242794901*^9, 3.968565274979278*^9}, {
   3.968565434254327*^9, 3.968565523080517*^9}, 3.968565588261168*^9, {
   3.968565719630509*^9, 3.968565789567175*^9}, {3.9685691741839943`*^9, 
   3.968569194233759*^9}, {3.968569301831994*^9, 3.968569352158897*^9}, {
   3.968569681897046*^9, 3.968569698084119*^9}, {3.968569832123639*^9, 
   3.968569856282352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9a3897a6-1bc9-42f3-9007-\
c1995d506be6"],

Cell["\<\
So maybe we can start by teaching logic and how something implies the other. \
It may enhance the AI\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]computational \
capabilities\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. Now, how does one even reach to the \
point of making something like that? Alpha proof uses reinforcement learning \
in lean to understand those tactics. It is trained on many examples. How can \
we teach an AI basic stuff like \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]for all\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]there exists\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], etc. just set theory. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s just \
start there. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968570436277313*^9, 3.968570471616522*^9}, {
  3.968570507423843*^9, 3.968570518432828*^9}, {3.9685705715385733`*^9, 
  3.968570608627541*^9}, {3.968570683651932*^9, 3.9685707126650867`*^9}, {
  3.968570747770321*^9, 
  3.968570818693695*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"792e9eb7-c04e-4252-872f-\
293365e7f686"],

Cell["", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4375f6a-ad14-422d-ae5b-27626d56e078"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Q1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968490531828397*^9, 
  3.968490536884411*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b040bdd8-56da-498f-a110-\
7fb4e9a9387c"],

Cell["\<\
Now, one can ask whether what is the sequence of things we can teach to the \
AI agent. I think that the sequence doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter and the \
knowledge state of the brain should just converge ultimately.  Now the point \
is we need to make something that can exploit the patterns that exist. It can \
be a neural net, or some connectivity type data structure etc.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968212234043585*^9, 3.968212329789113*^9}, {
  3.968212388787152*^9, 3.968212396600828*^9}, {3.9682124398382*^9, 
  3.968212468821333*^9}, {3.968216813087039*^9, 
  3.968216816603014*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0e702e73-2b2e-4510-9a06-\
440c32707edc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If I have image recognition, then it seems that there is a pattern \
without/input output with just input output data. well, \
that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not true. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s some categorisation \
which is at most injective and so there is a notion of output. we are putting \
things as similar...which is equivalent to putting some map and then some \
equaivalne relation...",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"A", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A", "/"}], "\[Tilde]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba4a6596-36ea-4847-a5e9-bf853b2038f5"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9684901008209677`*^9, 3.968490206003663*^9}, {
  3.968490238898471*^9, 3.968490273270289*^9}, {3.9684903846531143`*^9, 
  3.9684903852294397`*^9}, {3.968564979398447*^9, 3.9685649825547943`*^9}, {
  3.9685652863806334`*^9, 3.968565305462832*^9}, {3.968565384313298*^9, 
  3.968565385587229*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f58b03d2-6e5a-4560-9926-\
9986b7263250"],

Cell["\<\
SO it is all about the power of infinity. basically, the input set is is \
infinite. it is easy to learn a function of a finite domain by just \
evaluating the function on those inputs. However, we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
do it computationally for every thing. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968490430338065*^9, 3.9684904910269203`*^9}, {
   3.968496259053074*^9, 3.968496267912016*^9}, 
   3.9685714024054127`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c8adad8a-a6d0-41b5-9e4b-\
8415a9017c1e"],

Cell["\<\
So how does one test whether a computer program has \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]learned logic\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] well? \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968490511474092*^9, 
  3.968490526728718*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"af446dd2-34cd-45be-8e18-\
24fdaf79ed35"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Teach numbers and sets", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966921392794115*^9, 3.966921395481906*^9}, {
  3.967005988465591*^9, 
  3.96700599028307*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ddc39b64-8213-42c7-b8a4-\
622340d0ce7f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Random", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966922772968637*^9, 3.966922779953391*^9}, {
  3.96702721911661*^9, 
  3.967027221002782*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"67eae455-a446-4020-8623-\
00517b269ff3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ok. So assume that we are teaching the proof agent some mathematics. Now, \
it might be hard to just assume that it can prove things. We can try a \
smaller way to test whether it even understands a proof. That can be \
understanding the logical argument of the proof etc. Obviously, it will learn \
by doing as well, but that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a separate issue. Think of it \
this way: when we learn something, the knowledge gets \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]formed\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the brain. And then \
that structure keeps on changing, evolving, as we learn more and more. We get \
more confident and certain about patterns etc. and start forming \
correlations, causations, and other concepts in the mind. Thus, what we can \
start with is by making an AI proof understand certain proofs and the way to \
think mathematically ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9acfc3c2-b7ed-443b-9fe9-6500e178390c"],
 " which means there is a certain data structure/embedding of this knowledge \
in a way that helps it learn. That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s what I thought about \
the random walk. However, we can also try word embeddings/semantics as well. \
"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966926877604209*^9, 3.966926912777903*^9}, {
  3.966927397095286*^9, 3.96692740776665*^9}, {3.966927452899146*^9, 
  3.966927474762773*^9}, {3.966928911624121*^9, 3.966928973232563*^9}, {
  3.966929014069166*^9, 
  3.966929192615726*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c40a6b13-b11b-4ace-88a9-\
933fd5cedac9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Thus, if we are using neural nets, we can focus on first learning. I.e. the \
weights get adjusted as the AI learns new proofs and just reads more text. \
This can be thought of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]training data\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], however, here, there are no input/output labels. \
This reminds me of unsupervised learning. There are many such algorithms ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4734e633-3737-47dd-8d28-757137361355"],
 " like the Boltzmann machine etc. We can look at that. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
the same thing in the human brain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d446f38c-9bea-4732-b26c-10aeea8edca2"],
 " where the dots get connected slowly and slowly. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966977072458688*^9, 3.96697714073833*^9}, {
  3.966977173016957*^9, 3.966977189244681*^9}, {3.967003924488907*^9, 
  3.967003926254771*^9}, {3.9670039953697157`*^9, 3.967004007571832*^9}, {
  3.967004438744368*^9, 
  3.967004441292796*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ff2b3b48-7968-45c8-ab6a-\
49dc5fa54eb1"],

Cell["\<\
One simple thing we can do: we can try to embed these concepts in the mind.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967004982771084*^9, 3.967005003255666*^9}, {
  3.9670050811445436`*^9, 3.96700508730614*^9}, {3.96700533249256*^9, 
  3.967005337302115*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"056cac13-fa33-4241-b67b-\
1a8b4e12835d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So assume that the AI reads a proof. And then it can learn it i.e. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]store it in its memory\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. \
However, does it understand it? No. Because understanding it means that you \
can take understand the individual steps of the proof. However, that is a \
circular definition. Basically, it means that one can extrapolate the ideas \
from the proof and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]apply\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] them \
elsewhere. i.e. there is a sort of an embedding map into the landscape of \
mathematics ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dbf38345-a330-49a8-82b6-2db84fec4553"],
 " so in relation to something else. And the intuition is a sort of visual \
can be a sort of visual understanding. However, that is also a sort of an \
embedding. I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know. Weird.  there is so much fuzziness \
and data compression. Well, can it "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027723917636*^9, 3.967027735097439*^9}, {
  3.967027774032713*^9, 3.967027817729534*^9}, {3.967027907314958*^9, 
  3.967027909655468*^9}, {3.967028121134354*^9, 3.967028174267994*^9}, {
  3.967028244559647*^9, 3.967028260528818*^9}, {3.967028331987715*^9, 
  3.967028361113755*^9}, {3.967028433662732*^9, 
  3.967028435700536*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"945e2995-67e0-4c09-a27a-\
2e45e87892e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s do this. the reality of the situation is that this \
is a hard project. the purpose is to have some project or something when I \
apply for a job. A well ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e054df0a-5012-4268-971a-557bec09a3d2"],
 " documented github page. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967029702346922*^9, 3.967029703795876*^9}, {
  3.968397433481532*^9, 
  3.968397486435937*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"837d59c7-f3da-4b65-a623-\
2766ef5670e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (Learning). If an AI agent exists in a state, it can read a piece of \
mathematical text, and then its state changes. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 
  3.96702896118552*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a8c778c0-509a-4383-a6d8-\
2053066f96de"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Example.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " If an AI agent reads something, it can store the proof as a sequence of \
tokens in the English language and add it to its memory, which is a series of \
registers with one token in one register. It consists of everything it has \
read till now. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031134901812*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c08a5692-6d54-46c8-b554-\
033dbaf8f35d"],

Cell["\<\
This is not useful because here the AI doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t understand \
the proofs. Well, again...what if understanding comes later, after storing \
the data?Sure. but let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to come up with  a better data \
structure. Maybe again let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s be more abstract.\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 
  3.967031714882433*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cc230083-836b-4edc-bde0-\
859aeacee2a5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Example. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "If an AI agent reads something, it can store the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]most important\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] concepts about \
the proof, which are more relevant. It can consist of information like what \
concepts lead to others used in the proof. The concepts can be stored as \
mathematical objects in Lean and a structure such as a weighted directed \
hypergraph can be used to capture how those concepts are related. Thus, nodes \
might represent \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]math tokens\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
and a hierarchy of lemmas, theorems, definitions can be created."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.967031788329285*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032004633436*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"92d0762b-5e93-4c0f-beb2-\
2d2191d7a4a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is of course, lot of flexibility here. However, we need to make \
important decisions regarding the granularity of the tokens. Is there some \
partial order structure that is stored? Or some causal structure. DO i have a \
node named \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Zorn\[CloseCurlyQuote]s lemma\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and it leading to other proofs. A node of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]odd\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] being related to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], "  ", "+", " ", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"f8944f2f-b021-4893-8725-373f0443eaab"],
 ", and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]even\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] being related to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2a545011-439f-447c-b654-96634aec8716"],
 ". if so, do I store the actual definition of even = 2 k. Then, will the \
graph will be \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]connected\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
how will data be input? Also, if a question is asked, then how do we search \
in this incredibly large data space. It seems that as our knowledge grows, \
the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]access\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] time to the thought \
decreases."
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.967031788329285*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
  3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032481323991*^9}, {3.967098891129301*^9, 
  3.967098892912923*^9}, {3.9684905540340242`*^9, 3.968490554048313*^9}, {
  3.969454664147717*^9, 
  3.969454666353298*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"67ddd319-06a7-46a3-9499-\
30dcf5ab3a7a"],

Cell["\<\
This is better than the previous one, but still pretty basic. I think this \
attempts to recreate how the brain works, but is clearly not. Okay, the \
lookup problem can be solved in some way here: note that chat gpt solves that \
problem! here, neural nets are just input output relationships pre trained. \
thus, if the agent gets a question, the way it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gets\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] thre is by just getting trained and it knowing what \
to think in that siutation. so first we just train the neural net like that. \
maybe it will work? Maybe the loss function is some sort of miniizer of \
energy.\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.967031788329285*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
  3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032503635399*^9}, {3.967035973608824*^9, 
  3.967036036967684*^9}, {3.967098740345012*^9, 3.967098751788843*^9}, {
  3.967098786264683*^9, 
  3.967098790639669*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b54e36cc-423f-4f71-8316-\
c78a218d6c6a"],

Cell["\<\
This seems like  amajor simplification of how the brain actually works in the \
first place.\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
   3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
   3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
   3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
   3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
   3.9670317883292837`*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
   3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
   3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032503237895*^9}, {3.967033768566349*^9, 
   3.967033780939265*^9}, {3.967091707785918*^9, 3.967091707793621*^9}, 
   3.9670987354464297`*^9, {3.9684920044000587`*^9, 
   3.968492018101763*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5457b447-beff-45a3-9e79-\
a2b78749f9e0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s think of weirder models. The problem here is that \
of the search space. In the case of the neural nets, it can predict the next \
word by input output. it gets an input, and then it just applies the \
transformations (not heavy computationally) and then just outputs the next \
word. That is not how the brain works. man. Progress is difficult here. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.967031788329285*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
  3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032503237895*^9}, {3.967033768566349*^9, 
  3.967033780939265*^9}, {3.96709170901576*^9, 3.967091722303563*^9}, {
  3.967097751255919*^9, 3.967097759625136*^9}, {3.967097791864215*^9, 
  3.967097813801581*^9}, {3.967097868902622*^9, 3.967097955460798*^9}, {
  3.9670980145721483`*^9, 3.9670980245747223`*^9}, {3.967098337079814*^9, 
  3.967098345197523*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94f6db78-0264-4fd3-af3f-\
4994f2c7092f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Maybe the brain is a quantum state and it has equations of motion. And the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]thoughts\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are just the states \
of the brain upon measurement. This may explain the uncertainty or fuzziness \
in a certain way. There are multiple areas of research over here. However, \
what about the environment and free will?"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQA2IQ/cfRS7Wx763jZ/nrYDpo4gcLED3142xLEP2huW0n
iI7TW7gHRK9YkX4QRM/fG3MURG/suHYLRD+Y8uY2iE5jPf6oCUhXBKR8AtGd
/rONm4F0mMYrUxBd09llC6Ll/EMCQfQ7w5uhIHraomvRIHpdb1wNiD7z62s3
