B0SbfBHfC6J/iPz9DqLtLfP/gugLshksS0D+WX+cDUQbndulBKI3TjuiAaLv
HH/7di2Q9vgl8Q5EAwCO4MUr
  "],ExpressionUUID->"398cc355-5b29-410c-a740-52b70222a6a6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " What if the brain is not just a graph? as in it is some \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]operator\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and thoughts are the \
eigenvalues or something like that so that they are \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]immediately accessed\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. Anyway, \
I care about the mathematical world. So the only issue now is that if there \
is an input then the thought produced by the brain is not a search: it is \
literally the brain \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]acting\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] on \
that thought giving that thing. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBmIQ/cfRS7Wx763jZ/nrYDpo4gcLED3142xLEP2huW0n
iI7TW7gHRK9YkX4QRM/fG3MURG/suHYLRD+Y8uY2iE5jPf6oCUhXBKR8AtGd
