  "],ExpressionUUID->"f58725cb-f191-4edc-951f-0a4e31d3ec67"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The associative model seems very basic. The fact that memory is associative \
and connections get strainghtened over time can be thought of literally from \
a graph standpoint. However, there can be a more abstract realization of \
this. If we think about memory in chunks then it may not work. Memory may be \
a higher order structure (a sheaf or something). "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGCQAGIQ/cfRS7Wx763jZ/nrYDpo4gcLED3142xLEP2huW0n
iI7TW7gHRK9YkX4QRM/fG3MURG/suHYLRD+Y8uY2iE5jPf6oCUhXBKR8AtGd
