3Z6DgWXBNRVkUt/08HuSfodJLUcRC8Qlwl0i12krh+P8MRpKc7T1ULNx2Azj
s10Rq16YdlhqWpZDOtkbthCpKz/bShSMMA2VCyGR28CRwQJBej+8aJUMQ/2z
XQGDbT8aGHu64oG/vTNeGPi4MXcTDQ5mCSbEDXJ68Fs4MTBNmcOFHkEWHxZ3
1J1A6nQsotZ1mNuH7/zfP5MwCd4=
  "],ExpressionUUID->"404160e3-94a5-4b08-935e-b4e5396ce315"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Example.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Maybe something that is very underlying. Something that has the ability to \
extract higher order features from different systems which enables the study \
of regularities,"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.9670317883292837`*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
  3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032503237895*^9}, {3.967033768566349*^9, 
  3.9670338081322746`*^9}, {3.9674456984730587`*^9, 3.967445698476678*^9}, {
  3.967504089725348*^9, 3.967504112711658*^9}, {3.967508941353652*^9, 
  3.967508944075101*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bb3b43cc-36f3-4277-9fe8-\
081f8ddc3b4c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " I think what is important is that we can formalise this idea of not \
knowing enough and seeing the higher order patterns. For instance, in \
metamathematical space, we can think of theorems as paths in a graph. So now, \
if we look at the nodes of the graph in detail and prove everything in set \
theory, things become difficult. However, if we look at the higher idea, \
things seem simpler. Somehow, associations make things simpler."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
  3.96702870903691*^9}, {3.967028747239338*^9, 3.967028778898147*^9}, {
  3.967028950704186*^9, 3.967028959393173*^9}, {3.967031062219409*^9, 
  3.967031187134823*^9}, {3.967031708853459*^9, 3.967031727317424*^9}, {
  3.9670317883292837`*^9, 3.967031946634658*^9}, {3.967031982787345*^9, 
  3.967032030707347*^9}, {3.967032290954795*^9, 3.967032415686865*^9}, {
  3.967032456734853*^9, 3.967032503237895*^9}, {3.967033768566349*^9, 
  3.9670338081322746`*^9}, {3.967508870081457*^9, 3.967508874031052*^9}, {
  3.967508966517735*^9, 3.9675090806352053`*^9}, {3.967509189413134*^9, 
  3.967509230182474*^9}, {3.9675092690536547`*^9, 
  3.9675093044953337`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8b2bf415-ced7-4684-bf90-\
1ce2809a8b2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We may understand how to think about concepts. Because there must be \
something ",
 StyleBox["physical ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "about an idea i.e. a physical realization of intelligence."
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967027498320555*^9, 3.96702750272265*^9}, {
  3.96702765551774*^9, 3.96702766087324*^9}, {3.967028684203605*^9, 
