Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Teach group theory", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966571301964355*^9, 
  3.966571304703677*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c7d62167-17ac-48a8-aa0a-\
bc5a4c797f84"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Can we teach an AI group theory? How will it solve a group theory problem \
if it sees some problems before? Come on. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s do this.  \
Maybe if I attack the problem then I will see how it works over here. \
Question: show that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["b", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
     SuperscriptBox["a", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a888ee4c-e178-4656-8a25-9bc36ec85064"],
 ". Now, I know that the question is well",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "277443a1-29d9-4621-8e39-2a5ab7c30f90"],
 "defined because inverses are unique based on the previous theorem that the \
inverses are unique. So there is some English understanding and some \
visualisation over here going on. Maybe association thing.  I have the \
spatial understanding that inverse is something inverts things and so we get \
the identity so i try to multiply it. And the idea that the inverse \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
matter slowly gets strengthened."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966571306890881*^9, 3.966571329069873*^9}, {
  3.966572464441924*^9, 3.966572467993466*^9}, {3.966574899634088*^9, 
  3.966574914756133*^9}, {3.9665750668493643`*^9, 3.96657512611534*^9}, {
  3.966575177474209*^9, 3.966575217318499*^9}, {3.966575302048925*^9, 
  3.966575328044863*^9}, {3.966632335795022*^9, 3.966632335958671*^9}, {
  3.9669245070902*^9, 
  3.9669245088909283`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e2aba431-896d-43cc-a3d5-\
291aebe4aabf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "now, how can we make an AI to do these proofs? We can use the LLMs. Now the \
reason that chat gpt works is because there are so many degrees of freedom \
and there is regularity in the human language. But I think that there is \
regularity in mathematical proofs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "390fc51a-c311-47d5-8ac6-5a04f8c97f90"],
 " atleast in certain disciplines. If humans can do math, then so can AI. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966575332250708*^9, 3.966575348772099*^9}, {
  3.966575478633563*^9, 3.9665755496923447`*^9}, {3.966576360837915*^9, 
  3.966576403622967*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"374628c9-ce6a-4d90-a051-\
3055ae9f72af"],

Cell["\<\
AI must be smarter than humans because we have to create 1 AI. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966576404969534*^9, 
  3.966576416686398*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a09e1dc2-a3dd-4824-866c-\
f2d2d0adf51f"],

Cell["\<\
Seems there are some restrictions that I am facing. Well, they are not real. \
Like all that shit. We will need a different model. A large language model is \
just a transformer with extra degrees of freedom. So actually, attention is \
all we need in the case of this. What about in the case of proofs? The idea \
about proofs is that there are a finite number of theorems etc. we want to \
prover. however, there is some sort of regularity which allows us to choose \
those specific paths. there are certain human like traits when proving them, \
and we can add extra weights there. Okay. let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try this. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.966576902268431*^9, {3.96657693864388*^9, 3.966576956009206*^9}, {
   3.966577200872614*^9, 3.966577203653222*^9}, {3.966577246535739*^9, 
   3.966577342259273*^9}, {3.966577373787451*^9, 3.9665773949747753`*^9}, {
   3.966578182862666*^9, 
   3.966578183264236*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"254a1244-9e6a-4996-86e1-\
a67bc11aec09"],

Cell["\<\
Idea chasing. Ok. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to build a neural net here. \
Hmm.Well, let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try to build this AI algorithm.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966578197920368*^9, 3.9665782035476522`*^9}, {
  3.966578264580247*^9, 
  3.966578293913625*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0b5ba36e-a2b9-4527-b244-\
c2c60da2e308"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Question.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Show that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["b", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
     SuperscriptBox["a", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "19f2764b-d475-45ff-aa94-e3801d81d132"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  Try the pattern here. So here I look at the definition because I know I \
can just try what an inverse is. I have that spatial encoding of two things \
coming together and annihilating each other."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966632340526435*^9, 3.9666323599958353`*^9}, {
   3.966632793068064*^9, 3.9666328290404863`*^9}, {3.966632944588984*^9, 
   3.966632965727189*^9}, 
   3.966666152270282*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c22fd376-60a8-4352-892e-\
5878fbcb24b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Question.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Find all the subgroups of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ]", ",", "+"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ebe02f3e-0f0b-4deb-a4cb-dc51bf7f6f28"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966632967218445*^9, 3.9666329705614443`*^9}, {
  3.9666331980249863`*^9, 
  3.966633224577614*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e2039c24-ae74-47c8-afc4-\
889259e6686f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Proof. ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "I would look for examples. I know that there are some restrictions because \
a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]subgroup\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] has to have \
inverses and other things. So I try to find some example again. And then \
realise has to do with minimality. So then it goes at the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]back of my mind\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ee6a1792-ad04-4e29-a4ea-c3f9227c11e6"],
 " about minimality and division algorithm."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966633226826419*^9, 3.966633229756692*^9}, {
  3.966633318730969*^9, 3.96663334924501*^9}, {3.966633587549047*^9, 
  3.966633592878045*^9}, {3.966633724731989*^9, 3.966633739635124*^9}, {
  3.966633781256796*^9, 3.96663384571067*^9}, {3.9666341229844728`*^9, 
  3.966634123257968*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e3ed4483-f943-421c-97a1-\
aa3958a0db69"],

Cell["\<\
The idea is how to build up this intuition or pattern recognition or whatever \
you want to call it? Well, chat gpt also has that intuition and pattern \
recognition. It has so many weights etc. about the weight embeddings. And it \
all done using neural nets and some extra degrees of freedom (transformer). \
So it seems that neural nets should be able to do the job. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966633847823202*^9, 3.9666338576518917`*^9}, {
  3.966633986974175*^9, 3.966634008786581*^9}, {3.9666340771754713`*^9, 
  3.966634126132773*^9}, {3.966634225489791*^9, 
  3.966634235094282*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"39ee196d-87dd-4c31-977d-\
2b43e9977a18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(Group homomorphism). ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], " ", ")"}], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "(", "a", ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", "b", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c5fe6c-2b02-42ac-b6c0-a30f7e2efe4d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96663423752431*^9, 
  3.966634280048403*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"573dee34-50e9-4713-a26c-\
09c4edead3e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How can an AI ",
 StyleBox["understand ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "this definition? Well, again, understanding is encoded in various forms of \
information in the brain. visual, sound, different senses. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666515432760477`*^9, 3.966651547175899*^9}, {
  3.96665158350393*^9, 3.966651630369514*^9}, {3.966651661085217*^9, 
  3.966651664647129*^9}, {3.96665199800103*^9, 3.96665200508777*^9}, {
  3.966652265262549*^9, 3.966652285451174*^9}, {3.966654047187049*^9, 
  3.966654050610251*^9}, {3.966654111989099*^9, 
  3.966654119775119*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"715a4859-75d8-4a56-aa23-\
51d5e05493d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Question.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Show that homs send identity to identity."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96665413754671*^9, 3.966654148167725*^9}, {
  3.9666549521764307`*^9, 
  3.9666549530155983`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a2b4770-2a49-4324-9084-\
a7d905819af3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At first while learning, it may be difficult to understand and proof this. \
However, I know that after bunch of trying, it should be easy to show this \
and prove this. So from experience, i know that showing something is the \
identity means that it satifies that axiom. And then i see that i can that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "(", "e", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ddfdd81c-6585-43f1-9e26-f16cefaa9f5f"],
 " is idempotent. ANd then in a group, an idempotent must the identity."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666541508468513`*^9, 3.966654174861363*^9}, {
   3.966654214608618*^9, 3.96665428742422*^9}, 3.966654883646089*^9, {
   3.966654934585141*^9, 
   3.966654950928056*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2b1cd232-ad2f-49fe-96a7-\
60253de2981d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Proposition. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Cyclic groups are abelian"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666549852325153`*^9, 
  3.966655002398921*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"78a398fe-42ce-47c8-bae8-\
9d38a100c7a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". this will come from associativity and so yes follow from the fact that \
integers are abelian under addition. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966655003419149*^9, 3.966655072932467*^9}, 
   3.966655203120184*^9},ExpressionUUID->"184c30a0-81b2-423a-8856-\
a415efaba7df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come up with a mathematical theory of this. Okay. \
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s try. The first attempt is to create some sort of an \
associative, dynamic memory with certain connections relating to different \
concepts being strengthened. So for instance, the inverse. As an AI reads the \
proof, it should understand what actually is an inverse element ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "306708ad-31d1-4464-bd72-116c55469ffd"],
 " something that annihilates the element and gives us the identity. And then \
showing examples of integers etc. should \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]help\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the AI understand because it is \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]related\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] to the concept of an \
inverse i..e the negative sign. In humans, there is a sense of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]relief\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or ease when we read \
this example because otherwise the concept of an inverse seems abstract and \
showing us an example helps because we are already familiar with integers. \
Showing this example to someone who is not familiar with integers won\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t help. So somehow integers are \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]well-connected\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the brain \
and adding an inverse as a negative sign connects the abstract notion of an \
inverse with the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]region\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
belonging to the integers."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966655289388921*^9, 3.966655290128125*^9}, {
  3.966659445291443*^9, 3.966659453579818*^9}, {3.9666597376328*^9, 
  3.96665976442063*^9}, {3.966659908421136*^9, 3.966659981224961*^9}, {
  3.966660030358927*^9, 3.966660059055921*^9}, {3.96666021883505*^9, 
  3.966660438432983*^9}, {3.966660520510021*^9, 
  3.966660575901259*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5fbcaab9-ba72-44b5-87a0-\
9e2741c9d71b"],

Cell["Knowledge is loss in entropy. Hmm. ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96666045241125*^9, 
  3.966660458907955*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"624e63dc-a8ad-4ff5-a727-\
4bdcda65ade8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that there is a whole ",
 StyleBox["stack of intelligence ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "that I have created which enables me to understand this. So again, it might \
be about how big the brain is and it might take time. It is very possible \
that language also ",
 StyleBox["drives ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "the understanding. So using ChatGPT as a side component might be relevant. \
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s come up with a mathematical theory of associative \
learning. Now, it can be in the form of numbers or something etc. I think a \
theory where there is certain abstract framework, then we can deal with \
different mathematical structures. For example, we may not even need numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f8724d6a-3891-41eb-a3f5-7a8afff0bf7c"],
 " there are many algorithms with graphs and other discrete structures. Thus, \
it can be a matter of what dynamical systems are useful. For instance, there \
are many theories involving operator algebra approaches to dynamics etc. It \
may be useful to arrive a very algebraic understanding of all these concepts. \
 There are various mathematical approaches that can help one abstract away \
the important things. And there are tons of resources where one can deal with \
this and come up with a notion. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966659991192639*^9, 3.966660028108858*^9}, {
   3.966660164232356*^9, 3.966660183135982*^9}, {3.96666611667976*^9, 
   3.966666143399538*^9}, {3.966670179679317*^9, 3.966670255471679*^9}, {
   3.966670328463802*^9, 3.966670350545802*^9}, {3.966670440924557*^9, 
   3.96667045475872*^9}, {3.966670617353937*^9, 3.966670656902532*^9}, {
   3.966670781240768*^9, 3.9666707913450403`*^9}, {3.9666715126416287`*^9, 
   3.966671517502322*^9}, 
   3.966740537535018*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d4599786-7cbe-4b11-81cd-\
6e8f86428fb1"],

Cell["\<\
All one has to do is to encode the idea that information exists and there are \
some relations between things. May have some information theory or something? \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966740481589767*^9, 3.966740498099819*^9}, {
  3.966740633574018*^9, 
  3.966740648129014*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7efbde14-37ee-4d05-8d6c-\
d1bf3a98f315"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(Knowledge category).",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "A knowledge category is a category ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[ScriptCapitalK]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0a42896a-3ff2-4be0-a132-de55a02a6bb3"],
 " where each object represents the state of a brain and morphisms are just \
modifications to that object."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671869422076*^9}, {3.966671944433725*^9, 
  3.966671944434857*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a3701a39-68ce-40ad-9697-\
3ae57c6bc232"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every category is a knowledge category. Does it have a terminal object ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4e2f4ade-f841-4f9c-be0f-56bee7708458"],
 " god? Has all knowledge. Or nothing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "768c4f87-0593-4ffa-a9f7-dcac3d690a3a"],
 " where nothing really exists. Here, morphisms just represent time and \
compositions are just "
}], "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671869422076*^9}, {3.9666719450939913`*^9, 3.966671987730645*^9}, {
  3.966672057038394*^9, 
  3.966672074094309*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d63dae99-05eb-48ea-8249-\
bd899708fd94"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Example. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The set of all neural networks forms a knowledge category  where a morphism \
is a modification of the weights etc. i.e. a step in the gradient descent. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671942798354*^9}, {3.966672020242608*^9, 
  3.9666720797574253`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2b377ce5-2c14-4a6c-ade7-\
a9ed41b1dbc4"],

Cell["\<\
Using an API is a morphism? It may not be useful to think about these things \
haha. \
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671942798354*^9}, {3.966672020242608*^9, 3.966672054870279*^9}, {
  3.966672334744354*^9, 3.966672334745245*^9}, {3.9666723783165693`*^9, 
  3.966672382384624*^9}, {3.966718411935546*^9, 3.96671842759938*^9}, {
  3.96674123885576*^9, 
  3.966741240190539*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a7e4f22e-5ac5-417f-bbe5-\
e848fe1d8978"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(Intelligence).",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Intelligence is the ability to find regularities in a complex system by \
interacting with the system and/or getting feedback from it."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671942798354*^9}, {3.966672020242608*^9, 3.966672054870279*^9}, {
  3.96667233557206*^9, 3.966672337374854*^9}, {3.966672373666333*^9, 
  3.9666723766124167`*^9}, {3.966741292770586*^9, 3.966741293803418*^9}, {
  3.9667413245423813`*^9, 3.966741325480653*^9}, {3.966771412296574*^9, 
  3.966771460989421*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e60bdc63-1908-4375-a7bd-\
155e91887bb0"],

Cell["\<\
This means there exists regularities in the structure right? what does that \
mean? Regularities can mean a lot of things depending on the mathematical \
framework. It can be continuity. It can mean a probability distribution or \
the ability to ensure correctness with time on average. Something like that. \
\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671942798354*^9}, {3.966672020242608*^9, 3.966672054870279*^9}, {
  3.96667233557206*^9, 3.966672337374854*^9}, {3.966672373666333*^9, 
  3.9666723766124167`*^9}, {3.966741292770586*^9, 3.966741293803418*^9}, {
  3.9667413245423813`*^9, 3.966741325480653*^9}, {3.966771412296574*^9, 
  3.966771460835639*^9}, {3.9667718026881647`*^9, 3.966771860054384*^9}, {
  3.966827662914912*^9, 3.966827709288272*^9}, {3.966827742440052*^9, 
  3.966827762501432*^9}, {3.966827855014963*^9, 
  3.966827857114826*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"832ffdd0-a72c-4770-968f-\
c78499026123"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "(Intuition). A consequence of intelligence. The confidence of knowing the \
regularity and acting on it.  Skipping ahead."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
  3.966671942798354*^9}, {3.966672020242608*^9, 3.966672054870279*^9}, {
  3.96667233557206*^9, 3.966672337374854*^9}, {3.966672373666333*^9, 
  3.966672376612417*^9}, {3.966741292770586*^9, 3.966741293803418*^9}, {
  3.9667413245423813`*^9, 3.966741325480653*^9}, {3.966771412296574*^9, 
  3.966771460835639*^9}, {3.9667718026881647`*^9, 3.966771860054384*^9}, {
  3.966827911795401*^9, 3.966827960685045*^9}, {3.966828025005661*^9, 
  3.966828025010747*^9}, {3.966828057524797*^9, 
  3.966828059794242*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"664b7e03-6ac1-4972-93c0-\
5b38a0bdd34b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Different ways of encoding information: visual, text, sound, touch etc. Who \
knows. Can increase the connectivity over here. Images or dynamics movements \
in the head encoding some form of information."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9666715286271152`*^9, 3.96667153054558*^9}, {
  3.966671758611851*^9, 3.966671802498605*^9}, {3.966671845037709*^9, 
