El80nRVECyc9O+gGpGU4mY+C6Ab9z6x+QFr6lCc7iF6pFKMHoufyzzQH0QD6
A8xK
  "],ExpressionUUID->"56a41cc5-564f-47a0-8320-58b0ddee8e2b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Exploration",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a3701ed-71f0-4594-a161-325c6cf77fa9"],
 "Exploitation tradeoff."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966751905513137*^9, 3.9667519185008307`*^9}, 
   3.9667520338720512`*^9, {3.9668311087326393`*^9, 3.966831110152644*^9}, {
   3.966832448563418*^9, 3.966832474014271*^9}, {3.966832537340046*^9, 
   3.966832537533579*^9}, {3.966832591988418*^9, 3.96683261433267*^9}, {
   3.966833170386035*^9, 
   3.966833171667725*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"33919a9a-fea5-4343-885a-\
572906204631"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A lot of ideas have been discovered before. Related to things like Hopfield \
neural networks, Boltzmann machines, and other things. So we can study these \
things as well. Now I m not doing a lot of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]coding\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6e2b072-e312-4b3a-b63a-17985d380eae"],
 " whatever that means. Well, programming experience etc. and designing these \
neural nets is an art and requires experience. Like using APIs and C++, Java \
etc. are useful. We can start with easy (toy) versions of this..reasoning."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966759347191654*^9, 3.966759352723984*^9}, {
  3.966834890496559*^9, 3.966834907911666*^9}, {3.966835069895195*^9, 
  3.966835118655334*^9}, {3.966835349458906*^9, 3.9668353576184807`*^9}, {
  3.966835404678536*^9, 3.9668354207885723`*^9}, {3.966835832126996*^9, 
  3.966835849075644*^9}, {3.966862648821747*^9, 
  3.9668626635556717`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0d065e0a-20a7-42a5-8d3e-\
e009b03e63ed"],

Cell["\<\
Idea is computation  + neural nets + other things. Idea might be to use \
neural nets but to predict the next \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]big idea\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the proof. Maybe making it associative in nature \
or something like that. I think a lot has to do with these attractors etc. \
The idea is to not replicate the brain but to make a model, however that will \
be. Maybe here the thoughts will just be semantic information or something. \
Well, that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s what those word vectors are. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQAWIQfcTO4YhG31vH+YxvjoPoA4KFDNpAms3ClxFEzzFO
FAbRMy7bSIFo9TupiiD654IqMC32yuWHPpA+bn31J4g2az7zF0SvqFvDYACk
01RvsIHorpvRnCD6xonZvCD6d4umMIi2uSGpDaLXNSQZgGgLK20zEP3g9H4L
EO03Pc0XRDOskg8C0XGP1CeDaDcXy/kg2ixUZyVY/YvoVSD6V3LIRhAdsaME
TGeu/nUORPMoJVwF0U7LqxQcgfS+hNmKIPpCfsQ5N5C6kIhLIJpJKfeaD5Ce
7uZxHURf8Vz9GESfeln5FES/mVjzEUTPL132GUQDAP36nOA=
  "],ExpressionUUID->"0a22fc97-30b7-4248-9397-449f59229e2e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "I mean, there are many different proof ",
 StyleBox["strategies and tactics. ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Now, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not just about proof strategy and tactic. It\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s about so many unsaid things i.e. learning from example."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966920613157118*^9, 3.9669206650818253`*^9}, {
  3.9669208066811543`*^9, 
  3.9669208108770523`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0a60fc81-d770-423f-89b9-\
85b12e4ddeee"],

Cell["\<\
So let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s use this model. Basically, thoughts are entangled \
in some weird way. And so yeah. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9669211207028513`*^9, 3.9669211294159613`*^9}, {
  3.966921171176499*^9, 
  3.966921178624352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1051e714-df5f-4bcc-8bf7-\
5cec6b2d4960"]
}, Closed]],

